siness intelligence, analytics, and data science, and market research and insights; and back-office services, such as finance and accounting, human resources, audit, and procurement services. In addition, it provides education services to 20 university partners. Grand Canyon Education, Inc. was formerly known as Significant Education, Inc. and changed its name to Grand Canyon Education, Inc. in August 2005. The company was founded in 1949 and is headquartered in Phoenix, Arizona.","ceo_bio":"Mr. Brian E. Mueller | Chairman & CEO | Age 71 | Compensation: $809,199 (FY2025)","culture_narrative":"Governance score flags moderate compensation governance risk (5/10).","financial_summary":["Grand Canyon Education, Inc. is a mid-cap consumer defensive business with a $3.0B market cap on $1.1B of annual revenue.","The top line has compounded at +7% over the past three years and +4% annually across the full decade, a respectable pace for a business of this size.","Returns on capital run at 42% against a 9% cost of capital \u2014 a 33-point spread that is the clearest signature of an economic moat.","The business throws off $239M in free cash flow \u2014 roughly 22 cents on every revenue dollar, which is the owner-earnings figure that actually belongs to shareholders, and cash conversion sits at 1.27\u00d7 so those profits are backed by real cash.","On the balance sheet, the balance sheet carries net cash, which is the gold standard: the business never has to make desperate decisions in a bad year.","Management returns a meaningful 8.8% of market cap to owners through dividends and buybacks, a strong signal of disciplined capital allocation, and insiders hold 2.2% of the shares, and within its sector the business captures 3.0\u00d7 its fair share of profits, a structural advantage visible in the numbers."],"sector_headwinds":[{"text":"Low reinvestment-driven growth suggests the compounding engine has stalled","sev":"amber","cat":"growth"},{"text":"Above-average short interest at 8.8% of float","sev":"amber","cat":"sentiment"},{"text":"Above-average market volatility (VIX 26)","sev":"amber","cat":"macro"},{"text":"Late-cycle dynamics increase the probability of a slowdown","sev":"amber","cat":"macro"},{"text":"Slow-motion taste and channel shifts \u2014 private label, Gen-Z health preferences, or a DTC disruption can erode decade-old brand moats without a single dramatic quarter.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"},{"text":"Input cost inflation from agricultural commodities \u2014 when raw materials spike, pass-through pricing lags and margin compression is immediate.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"},{"text":"GLP-1 and health-trend demand destruction \u2014 weight-loss drugs and wellness shifts are structurally reducing consumption in snack, beverage, and packaged food categories.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"}],"sector_tailwinds":["Operating margins 17% above sector median \u2014 the quantitative trace of pricing power","Trading at a 36% margin of safety to estimated fair value \u2014 a real cushion against errors in the estimate","Market is pricing in lower growth than the company has historically delivered","Trading near the bottom of its 52-week range \u2014 the market is offering a discount","Altman Z comfortably in the safe zone \u2014 a fortress balance sheet on this measure","ROIC sits in the top quartile of Consumer Defensive peers \u2014 the moat is wider than the neighbourhood","Consumer Defensive sector showing strong relative momentum, outperforming the market by 11% over 3 months","Consumer Defensive ETF in a sustained uptrend above its long-term average","Consumer Defensive tends to hold up well as investors rotate into defensive names"],"news_headlines":[{"title":"Grand Canyon Education (LOPE) Stock Still Looks Like A Bargain Following A 51% Run","source":"simplywall.st","link":"https://simplywall.st/stocks/us/consumer-services/nasdaq-lope/grand-canyon-education/news/grand-canyon-education-lope-stock-still-looks-lik